    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Footnote",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "/images/concept/tautology/indiana/CharlesDemuth28TFgre5InGold.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "width": "150",
      "height": "182",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Charles Demuth:\n\nThe Figure Five in Gold, 1928",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Great Figure",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Among the rain\n\nand lights\n\nI saw the figure 5\n\nin gold\n\non a red\n\nfire truck\n\nmoving\n\ntense\n\nunheeded\n\nto gong clangs\n\nsiren howls\n\nand wheels rumbling\n\nthrough the dark city",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "William Carlos Williams\n\n[In: Sour Grapes, 1921]",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Exam question",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "\"Is Missisippi Mississippi? Is there a Petula in Indiana?\"",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Ray Johnson: IS MARIANNE MOORE MARIANNE\nMOORE? (1966). In: Donna de Salvo and Catherine Gudis: Ray Johnson.\nCorrespondences. Columbus, Ohio: Wexner Center for the Arts,\n1999, pp. 169-171.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "[Answer: In William S. Wilson's accompanying essay: \"Ray Johnson: The One and the Other.\" (pp. 165-175).]",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Remko Scha. 2006",
      "links": []
    }
  ],
